1
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:04,140
The Closed tab lists the positions you have closed. It starts with the last day.

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,860
Click the period button to look further back.

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:16,390
Pick 5 Days, 1 Month or 6 Months, or Custom for your own dates.

4
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:19,250
Every position closed in that period is listed.

5
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:26,920
Reason shows why each one closed. Point at the heading to see every code.

6
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,280
C means you closed it yourself. S is a stop loss, L a take profit.

7
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:35,650
To see only some reasons, show the filter row.

8
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:40,370
Each code is listed with its meaning.

9
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:45,190
Select C and click the left arrow to hide the positions you closed yourself.

10
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:49,050
Now the stop loss and take profit closes are easy to see.

11
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:53,110
The arrow at the right of the status bar shows the rollover time and the clock.

12
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,670
Click it again to hide them.

